WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.303 --> 00:00:16.526
Nan and Rob's misadventure, Jo hoped for some quiet, trouble-free days.

2
00:00:18.068 --> 00:00:22.731
And things did remain peaceful until Tommy's hens caused a problem.

3
00:00:24.712 --> 00:00:28.015
Tommy had been steadily earning money from selling their eggs.

4
00:00:30.016 --> 00:00:33.118
But he spent his money so recklessly that Mr.

5
00:00:33.178 --> 00:00:35.419
Bauer insisted he start saving it.

6
00:00:37.961 --> 00:00:41.763
The professor gave Tommy a bank that was shaped like a miniature house.

7
00:00:41.783 --> 00:00:48.347
"After you've saved five dollars, you may open the bank, but you must spend the money wisely."

8
00:00:51.189 --> 00:00:55.392
Tommy soon had four dollars in the bank, which he kept under his bed.

9
00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:03.862
When Jo paid him another dollar for eggs, Tommy rushed to the barn to show Nat.

10
00:01:03.882 --> 00:01:07.643
"Look at these!"

11
00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:10.644
Tommy said, displaying four quarters.

12
00:01:10.664 --> 00:01:14.165
"Oh, I wish I had that dollar."

13
00:01:15.985 --> 00:01:21.707
Nat was still Tommy's partner in the egg business, but he always had fewer eggs to sell than

14
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:26.248
Tommy. "I'd add it to the money I'm saving for a violin."

15
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.801
"I have five dollars now, but I haven't decided how to spend it."

16
00:01:32.981 --> 00:01:36.302
Tommy tossed the shiny quarters in the air and caught them.

17
00:01:36.322 --> 00:01:39.043
"Maybe I'll lend you some."

18
00:01:39.063 --> 00:01:41.744
"Hey, everybody!"

19
00:01:42.124 --> 00:01:44.225
a voice called from outside the barn.

20
00:01:44.245 --> 00:01:47.206
"Dan just caught a huge snake!"

21
00:01:47.226 --> 00:01:49.266
"Come on, let's go!"

22
00:01:50.887 --> 00:01:55.492
Tommy was in too much of a hurry to put his money in his bank, so he hid

23
00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:58.274
the quarters under an old feed sack in the barn.

24
00:02:00.295 --> 00:02:05.018
The interesting snake made Tommy forget about his quarters until bedtime.

25
00:02:05.038 --> 00:02:09.280
"I'll get them tomorrow," he said to himself.

26
00:02:10.481 --> 00:02:13.142
"Nobody except Nat knows where they're hidden anyway."

27
00:02:16.364 --> 00:02:22.827
The next morning Tommy rushed into the schoolroom, crying, "Hey, which one of you has my money?"

28
00:02:26.874 --> 00:02:28.396
"What are you talking about?"

29
00:02:28.716 --> 00:02:29.517
Demi asked.

30
00:02:31.098 --> 00:02:35.162
Tommy described how he'd hidden the quarters under the old feed sack.

31
00:02:35.182 --> 00:02:38.585
"That's right," Nat said.

32
00:02:38.605 --> 00:02:40.666
"I saw him do it."

33
00:02:40.686 --> 00:02:45.531
"Somebody must have stolen the money," Jack said.

34
00:02:45.551 --> 00:02:54.154
"When I find out who did it," Tommy said, "I'll—" "Stay calm," Dan interrupted.

35
00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:59.397
"We'll figure this out because thieves usually give themselves away."

36
00:02:59.417 --> 00:03:02.699
"What's all this about thieves?"

37
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.702
the professor asked, coming into the schoolroom.

38
00:03:07.223 --> 00:03:09.264
Tommy explained the situation again.

39
00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:14.888
When he reached the part about hiding the money, everyone looked at Nat.

40
00:03:14.908 --> 00:03:19.631
"I know you think I stole it, but I didn't!"

41
00:03:20.111 --> 00:03:22.597
Nat cried, his face turning red.

42
00:03:22.617 --> 00:03:25.719
"Take your seats," Mr.

43
00:03:25.759 --> 00:03:26.520
Bauer said.

44
00:03:30.523 --> 00:03:34.426
going to ask each of you a question, and I want an honest answer.

45
00:03:35.066 --> 00:03:37.468
Don't make things worse for yourself by lying."

46
00:03:39.289 --> 00:03:44.933
Mr. Bauer questioned the boys one by one, and each boy denied taking the money.

47
00:03:46.454 --> 00:03:48.256
Finally it was Nat's turn.

48
00:03:50.368 --> 00:03:54.711
"Now, my boy, please give me an honest answer," the professor said.

49
00:03:54.731 --> 00:03:56.893
"Did you take the money?"

50
00:03:56.913 --> 00:03:59.615
"No, sir."

51
00:04:00.776 --> 00:04:05.199
Nat looked so miserable that the professor felt some compassion for him.

52
00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:07.461
But Mr.

53
00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:13.705
Bauer also knew that Nat had a history of lying, especially to keep himself out of trouble.

54
00:04:13.725 --> 00:04:21.134
"I'm very sorry, Nat, but the evidence is against you," the professor said gravely.

55
00:04:21.154 --> 00:04:25.897
"And the lies you've told in the past cause me to doubt you now.

56
00:04:28.658 --> 00:04:31.540
I'll give you another chance to tell the truth, if you want one.

57
00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.361
That's up to you and your conscience."

58
00:04:35.902 --> 00:04:38.984
"I didn't take the money I didn't!"

59
00:04:45.187 --> 00:04:46.048
Nat sobbed.

60
00:04:47.428 --> 00:04:52.011
He hung his head in shame because he couldn't bear to look at his friends.

61
00:04:54.032 --> 00:04:59.935
For the next week, Nat suffered a kind of slow torture as the other boys ignored him.

62
00:05:01.236 --> 00:05:04.978
Jo was as kind as ever, but she seemed disappointed in him.

63
00:05:06.559 --> 00:05:12.522
And the sad look in the professor's eyes broke Nat's heart because he loved his teacher dearly.

64
00:05:14.163 --> 00:05:17.548
One person who still believed in Nat was Daisy.

65
00:05:18.729 --> 00:05:22.010
When Nat played his fiddle, Daisy sat by his side.

66
00:05:23.491 --> 00:05:28.013
She made him special treats in her kitchen and brought him flowers from her garden.

67
00:05:30.454 --> 00:05:34.356
Dan also jumped to Nat's defense whenever anyone criticized him.

68
00:05:35.997 --> 00:05:40.799
After a while some of the boys began to doubt that Nat had taken the money.

69
00:05:43.732 --> 00:05:47.935
A rumor started circulating that Dan was behind the theft.

70
00:05:50.857 --> 00:05:56.641
One afternoon Nat encountered Dan watching insects gliding over the surface of the brook.

71
00:05:56.661 --> 00:06:02.486
"Thanks for sticking up for me," Nat said to his old friend.

72
00:06:02.506 --> 00:06:06.608
"I'm sorry that some people are accusing you of being the thief."

73
00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:11.472
Dan turned away from Nat, tossing a stone into the brook.

74
00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.121
"How do you know they're not right?"

75
00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:18.742
"Because you don't care about money!"

76
00:06:19.162 --> 00:06:20.303
Nat said fiercely.

77
00:06:20.323 --> 00:06:24.805
"All you're interested in are bugs and rocks and things."

78
00:06:24.825 --> 00:06:30.467
"I want a butterfly net as much as you want a fiddle," Dan said.

79
00:06:30.487 --> 00:06:33.208
"Why wouldn't I steal the money for it?"

80
00:06:34.369 --> 00:06:37.790
"You like to fight sometimes, but I don't believe you'd lie or steal."

81
00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:44.757
"Well, I've done both," Dan said, throwing another stone into the water.

82
00:06:44.777 --> 00:06:50.699
"I used to lie all the time, and I stole things to eat when I ran away from

83
00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:51.520
Mr. Page."

84
00:06:53.801 --> 00:06:55.962
"Oh, Dan, tell me it's not you!"

85
00:06:56.422 --> 00:06:57.843
Nat said in distress.

86
00:06:57.863 --> 00:07:01.344
"It's not me," Dan replied.

87
00:07:01.364 --> 00:07:05.726
"But don't worry—we'll figure out who the real culprit is."

88
00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:12.726
Nat studied Dan's face and said slowly, "I think you already know who it is.

89
00:07:14.207 --> 00:07:17.810
If you do, beg him to tell the truth because I don't think I can stand this much

90
00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:21.973
longer. If I were as brave as you are, I'd run away.

91
00:07:22.394 --> 00:07:25.196
But I'm not, so I have to wait for someone to tell the truth."

92
00:07:27.077 --> 00:07:34.123
"You won't have to wait much longer," Dan said, and then he quickly walked away and wasn't seen

93
00:07:34.223 --> 00:07:34.884
for hours.
